capability scan/tokens  a text read into its tokens, one after another, the end last
  heroes  scanner.scan, scanner.new_scanner, scanner.next_token, scanner.Scanner, scanner.Token, scanner.Kind
  go      text/scanner.Scanner, Scanner.Init, Scanner.Scan, text/scanner.GoTokens, go/scanner.Scanner, go/scanner.Scanner.Init, go/scanner.Scanner.Scan
  rust    logos::Logos (derive and trait), Logos::lexer, Logos::lexer_with_extras, logos::Lexer, Lexer::new, Lexer::with_extras, Lexer::next
  python  tokenize.tokenize, tokenize.generate_tokens, shlex.shlex, shlex.shlex.get_token, shlex.shlex.read_token, shlex.shlex.posix
  note    a text is read whole, where Go's `Init` takes an `io.Reader` and Python's `tokenize` bytes with their encoding; every kind Go's text/scanner reads, and what Go reads, matched over 20,000 generated texts and every combination of its modes against Go 1.27's text/scanner on 2026-11-18: each token's kind, text, offset, line and column and the first error of a malformed one alike, but for the two departures written in `scan/place` and `scan/strings`

capability scan/peek  the next token known before it is taken
  heroes  scanner.peek_token
  go      -
  rust    Lexer::clone (a copy read ahead)
  python  shlex.shlex.push_token
  note    Python's `push_token` gives back a token already taken; here the next one is seen before it is taken, which is the use of pushing back one

capability scan/characters  the characters between tokens read one at a time, or the next one looked at
  heroes  scanner.next_char, scanner.peek_char
  go      text/scanner.Scanner.Next, text/scanner.Scanner.Peek
  rust    Lexer::bump, Lexer::remainder
  python  -
  note    the end is `not_found`, where Go's `Peek` and `Next` answer EOF; Rust's `bump` lengthens the token, here a program reads the characters with `next_char` and makes its token of them

capability scan/rules-changed  the rules changed in the middle of a text, the place kept
  heroes  scanner.set_rules
  go      text/scanner.Scanner.Mode (set between calls), Scanner.Whitespace (set between calls), Scanner.IsIdentRune (set between calls)
  rust    Lexer::morph
  python  shlex.shlex.wordchars, shlex.shlex.whitespace, shlex.shlex.commenters (set between calls)

capability scan/place  where a token stands: its byte offset, line and column, at its start and at its end
  heroes  scanner.Place, scanner.Token, scanner.place_of, scanner.format_place
  go      text/scanner.Position, Position.Offset, Position.Line, Position.Column, Position.IsValid, Position.String, Scanner.Pos, Scanner.Position, go/token.Position, go/token.Pos, go/token.Pos.IsValid, go/token.NoPos, go/scanner.Scanner.End
  rust    Lexer::span, logos::Span, Lexer::spanned, logos::SpannedIter
  python  tokenize.TokenInfo, TokenInfo.start, TokenInfo.end, TokenInfo.line, shlex.shlex.lineno, shlex.shlex.error_leader
  note    lines from 1 and columns from 1 counted in characters, as Go's; Python counts its columns from 0. A place names no file, Go's `Filename`: the program that read the file names it. A byte order mark that begins the text is passed over and counted as a column, as Go does; the end of an empty text is at 1:1, where Go answers line 0 and column 0, a place it calls invalid

capability scan/token-text  the text of a token as it stands in the source
  heroes  scanner.Token
  go      text/scanner.Scanner.TokenText
  rust    Lexer::slice, Lexer::source
  python  TokenInfo.string, shlex.shlex.token
  note    its field `text`

capability scan/identifiers  names read by the program's rule of which characters begin one and which follow
  heroes  scanner.Rules, scanner.is_identifier_char
  go      text/scanner.ScanIdents, text/scanner.Ident, Scanner.IsIdentRune
  rust    #[regex] on a token (logos's derive)
  python  tokenize.NAME, shlex.shlex.wordchars
  note    the fields `identifiers` and `identifier_char`, which is Go's `IsIdentRune` and asked as Go asks it; a character that could begin an identifier is `other` where identifiers are not read, as Go answers it

capability scan/keywords  the identifiers a program reserves told apart from the others
  heroes  scanner.Rules, scanner.Kind
  go      go/token.Lookup, go/token.IsKeyword, go/token.Token.IsKeyword
  rust    #[token] on a token (logos's derive)
  python  tokenize.SOFT_KEYWORD
  note    the field `keywords` and the kind `keyword`; Go's and Python's lists are their own language's, and a program writes its own

capability scan/integers  integers in decimal, hexadecimal, octal and binary, digits grouped by `_`
  heroes  scanner.Rules, scanner.Kind
  go      text/scanner.ScanInts, text/scanner.Int
  rust    #[regex] on a token
  python  tokenize.NUMBER
  note    the field `integers` and the kind `integer`, in Go's forms and with its messages: "invalid digit '8' in octal literal", "'_' must separate successive digits"

capability scan/floats  floats with a point, an exponent, or a hexadecimal mantissa
  heroes  scanner.Rules, scanner.Kind
  go      text/scanner.ScanFloats, text/scanner.Float
  rust    #[regex] on a token
  python  tokenize.NUMBER
  note    the field `floats` and the kind `float`; where floats are read integers are too, as Go's `ScanFloats` holds `ScanInts`; no imaginary `i`, which Go's text/scanner does not read either

capability scan/strings  strings between quotes, with escapes
  heroes  scanner.Rules, scanner.Kind
  go      text/scanner.ScanStrings, text/scanner.String
  rust    #[regex] on a token
  python  tokenize.STRING, shlex.shlex.quotes, shlex.shlex.escape, shlex.shlex.escapedquotes
  note    the fields `string_quotes` and `multiline_strings` and the kind `string`; Go's escapes, `\` before the quote that opened the string and no other; Go's text/scanner takes the line end into a literal that a line end leaves unclosed, here the line end stays out of it, so that `keep_newlines` loses no line

capability scan/raw-strings  strings between quotes that read no escape and may span lines
  heroes  scanner.Rules, scanner.Kind
  go      text/scanner.ScanRawStrings, text/scanner.RawString
  rust    #[regex] on a token
  python  -
  note    the field `raw_quotes` and the kind `raw_string`

capability scan/character-literals  one character, or one escape, between quotes
  heroes  scanner.Rules, scanner.Kind
  go      text/scanner.ScanChars, text/scanner.Char
  rust    #[regex] on a token
  python  -
  note    the field `char_quotes` and the kind `character`

capability scan/comments  comments to the end of a line and between delimiters, skipped or kept as tokens
  heroes  scanner.Rules, scanner.Kind
  go      text/scanner.ScanComments, text/scanner.SkipComments, text/scanner.Comment, go/scanner.Mode, go/scanner.ScanComments
  rust    #[logos(skip)] with a comment's pattern
  python  tokenize.COMMENT, shlex.shlex.commenters
  note    the fields `line_comments`, `block_comment_open`, `block_comment_close` and `keep_comments`, and the kind `comment`; a block comment never closed is a token of the kind `invalid` even where comments are skipped, where Go reports it with the end

capability scan/nested-comments  block comments that nest, each opening closed by its own closing
  heroes  scanner.Rules
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    the field `nested_comments`, as Rust, Swift and Haskell nest theirs

capability scan/whitespace  the characters that separate tokens, skipped or kept as tokens
  heroes  scanner.Rules, scanner.Kind
  go      text/scanner.Scanner.Whitespace, text/scanner.GoWhitespace
  rust    #[logos(skip)], logos::skip, logos::Skip
  python  shlex.shlex.whitespace, shlex.shlex.whitespace_split
  note    the fields `whitespace` and `keep_whitespace` and the kind `whitespace`; any character may be white space, where Go's mask holds the first 64 code points alone

capability scan/newlines  line ends as tokens of their own
  heroes  scanner.Rules, scanner.Kind
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tokenize.NEWLINE, tokenize.NL
  note    the field `keep_newlines` and the kind `newline`; Python's NEWLINE and NL differ by whether the line held code, which a program reads from the token before

capability scan/operators  operators and punctuation from the program's list, the longest that stands there
  heroes  scanner.Rules, scanner.Kind
  go      -
  rust    #[token] on a token
  python  tokenize.OP, tokenize.EXACT_TOKEN_TYPES, TokenInfo.exact_type, shlex.shlex.punctuation_chars
  note    the field `operators` and the kind `operator`: the longest that begins at the place, by `strings.match_patterns_at` over an automaton compiled once by `new_scanner`

capability scan/classes  token classes of the program's own, each a pattern
  heroes  scanner.Rules, scanner.Kind
  go      -
  rust    #[regex] on a token, #[logos(subpattern)], logos::Filter, logos::FilterResult
  python  -
  note    the field `classes`, each a `regex.Regex`, and the kind `custom`: tried first, the longest match wins and the first of the list where two are as long, as logos takes the longest; a program decides what logos's `Filter` decides from the token it gets

capability scan/other  a character no rule reads, given as a token of its own
  heroes  scanner.Kind
  go      text/scanner.Scanner.Scan (a character answered as itself)
  rust    -
  python  tokenize.ERRORTOKEN
  note    the kind `other`; a NUL is a token of the kind `invalid`, "invalid character NUL", where Go reports that error on the token before it, which its look-ahead was reading

capability scan/errors  a malformed token as a value, with its reason and its place, the scan going on after it
  heroes  scanner.Kind, scanner.scan_checked
  go      text/scanner.Scanner.Error, Scanner.ErrorCount, go/scanner.Error, go/scanner.Error.Error, go/scanner.ErrorHandler, go/scanner.ErrorList, ErrorList.Add, ErrorList.Err, ErrorList.Error, ErrorList.Len, ErrorList.Reset, ErrorList.Sort, ErrorList.Less, ErrorList.Swap, ErrorList.RemoveMultiples, go/scanner.PrintError, go/scanner.Scanner.ErrorCount
  rust    #[logos(error)], Lexer::next (a `Result`)
  python  tokenize.TokenError, tokenize.ERRORTOKEN
  note    the kind `invalid` with its reason, the token's place being the error's; one reason a token, the first, where Go's text/scanner can report two

capability scan/kind-names  the name of a token's kind, for a message
  heroes  scanner.kind_name
  go      text/scanner.TokenString, go/token.Token.String
  rust    -
  python  tokenize.tok_name, token.tok_name

capability scan/end  the end of the text as a token
  heroes  scanner.Kind
  go      text/scanner.EOF
  rust    -
  python  tokenize.ENDMARKER
  note    the kind `end`, answered again at every call after it, as Go's EOF

capability scan/values  the value a literal token spells: a string unquoted, an integer, a float
  heroes  scanner.text_of, scanner.int_of, scanner.float_of
  go      strconv.Unquote, strconv.ParseInt, strconv.ParseFloat (beside the census, asked as oracles)
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    what Go's `strconv.Unquote`, `strconv.ParseInt` with base 0 and `strconv.ParseFloat` answer for the same literals, asked on 2026-11-18; a character literal's `\x` and octal escapes are its code point, as Go's compiler reads `'\xff'`, where `strconv.Unquote` answers the byte, which no `str` holds; an escape that spells no character or bytes that are not UTF-8 fail `not_text`

capability scan/indentation  the indentation of lines as tokens, Python's INDENT and DEDENT
  heroes  refused: the indentation of one language, which a program reads as the column of the first token after a line end, `keep_newlines` given
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tokenize.INDENT, tokenize.DEDENT, tokenize.tabsize

capability scan/encodings  a source's encoding found and decoded before it is read
  heroes  refused: a scanner reads a `str`, which is UTF-8; bytes of another encoding are read by `unicode/encodings` first, and a byte order mark that begins the text is passed over
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tokenize.detect_encoding, tokenize.open, tokenize.ENCODING, tokenize.BOM_UTF8, tokenize.cookie_re, tokenize.blank_re

capability scan/untokenize  tokens written back as a text
  heroes  built-in join
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tokenize.untokenize, tokenize.Untokenizer
  note    the texts of the tokens joined with "" are the text again where white space, line ends and comments are kept

capability scan/sources  a text read from a stream, or several sources stacked, as an include reads another file
  heroes  refused: a scanner reads a text whole; a stream is `io`'s, on the same layer as `scanner`, so a program reads it first, and it stacks scanners itself for a file that includes another
  go      text/scanner.Scanner.Init (an `io.Reader`), text/scanner.Position.Filename
  rust    logos::source::Source, logos::source::Chunk
  python  shlex.shlex.push_source, shlex.shlex.pop_source, shlex.shlex.sourcehook, shlex.shlex.infile, shlex.shlex.instream, shlex.shlex.source

capability scan/shell-words  a line read as the words a POSIX shell gives, and words quoted for one
  heroes  strings.split_shell
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  shlex.split, shlex.quote, shlex.join
  note    the words of a shell line are `strings`'; a word quoted for a shell, Python's `shlex.quote` and `shlex.join`, is `process.quote`'s

dropped  one language's own tokens and their tables, which a program names by its own `keywords` and `operators`
  go      go/token.Token, go/token constants (ILLEGAL to TILDE), Token.IsLiteral, Token.IsOperator, Token.Precedence, go/token.IsExported, go/token.IsIdentifier, go/token.LowestPrec, go/token.UnaryPrec, go/token.HighestPrec
  rust    -
  python  tokenize's and token's constants of Python's operators (AMPER to VBAREQUAL), FSTRING_START, FSTRING_MIDDLE, FSTRING_END, TSTRING_START, TSTRING_MIDDLE, TSTRING_END, TYPE_COMMENT, TYPE_IGNORE, ISTERMINAL, ISNONTERMINAL, ISEOF, NT_OFFSET, N_TOKENS

dropped  a table of files and of the offsets their lines begin at, where a program compiles many files into one space of positions: a token here carries its own line and column
  go      go/token.File (AddLine, AddLineColumnInfo, AddLineInfo, Base, End, Line, LineCount, LineStart, Lines, MergeLine, Name, Offset, Pos, Position, PositionFor, SetLines, SetLinesForContent, Size, String), go/token.FileSet (NewFileSet, AddExistingFiles, AddFile, Base, File, Iterate, Position, PositionFor, Read, RemoveFile, Write)
  rust    -
  python  -

dropped  the regular expressions a module is built of, and its debugging: plumbing
  go      -
  rust    Lexer::extras, logos::Logos::Extras
  python  tokenize.Name, Number, String, Comment, Whitespace, Funny, Special, PlainToken, PseudoToken, PseudoExtras, Intnumber, Decnumber, Hexnumber, Octnumber, Binnumber, Floatnumber, Pointfloat, Expfloat, Exponent, Imagnumber, ContStr, Double, Double3, Single, Single3, Triple, StringPrefix, Ignore, endpats, single_quoted, triple_quoted, group, any, maybe, tokenize.TextIOWrapper, tokenize.lookup, shlex.shlex.debug, shlex.shlex.state, shlex.shlex.eof, shlex.shlex.pushback, shlex.shlex.filestack
